# {{name}}

> Plugin skeleton, generated once by `brickie new`. Afterwards **maintained by hand**.

> The ability `subkind` decides the phase: scheduler→early / framework·io·fs→core / service→late.

## Declaration surface (single source of truth)

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Plugin category `plugin_type` | `ability` |
| `subkind` | `{{subkind}}` |
| `api_type` | `{{api_type}}` |
| Language `lang` | `{{lang}}` (v0.1 ships c only) |
| Initial phase `phase` | `{{phase}}` (derived from plugin_type/subkind, `1-01` §6.2) |
| Initial version | `{{version}}` = `COMPAT_GEN.MAJOR.MINOR.REVISE` |

Field semantics: `docs/4-plugin/4-03-plugin-manifest.md`; v0.1 schema:
`docs/2-toolchain/brickie/brickie-v0.1.md` §8.1.

## Next steps (v0.1 loop)

> The tool itself is still under development — for current progress and per-command schedules see
> `docs/2-toolchain/brickie/checklist.md` §5.2.

```sh
brickie check                       # declaration-surface completeness check (composition-time validation)
brickie dep add {{name}} <dep>       # declare a structural dependency
brickie iface publish {{name}}       # publish the interface surface → hash + version bump
brickie gen                         # rebuild build/gen/** from brick.toml; --check only compares
```

`build/gen/{{name}}/plugin_desc.c` is a **generated file**, do not edit by hand — change `brick.toml`, then rebuild.

## Scope limits

v0.1 `check` is a **declaration-surface completeness checker** — it guarantees "this composition is logically consistent",
**not** that "it compiles / runs correctly" (no compiler, no symbol table, no QEMU).
